            "question": "My house is in a very high fire hazard severity zone. Can I use glass railing?",
            "answer": "<p>Much of the Hollywood Hills, Pacific Palisades and the foothills above Pasadena is mapped as a very high fire hazard severity zone. The California code has rules there for exterior building elements. Tempered glass and 2205 stainless steel do not burn, but the deck is usually wood, so check with LADBS and the fire authority. Homes being rebuilt in Pacific Palisades after the 2025 fire go through the same review.</p>",
