          "settings": {
            "question": "Do rooftop terraces in Venice or Manhattan Beach follow the same 42-inch rule?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The California code sets 42 inches as the minimum guard height, and the rule covers roof decks too. Venice is in the City of Los Angeles, so LADBS issues the permit. Manhattan Beach, Hermosa Beach and Santa Monica have their own building departments, fees and forms. The 46-inch panel, which gives 48 inches, is a common choice on an open roof.</p>",
            "pages": ""
